<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tippecanoe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1811</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumsehs-war">Tecumseh's War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tippecanoe was fought on 7 November 1811 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophetstown">Prophetstown</a>, in present-day Indiana, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> forces under Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-henry-harrison">William Henry Harrison</a> and warriors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumseh">Tecumseh</a>'s confederacy, led in his absence by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenskwatawa">Tenskwatawa</a>. Harrison's army repelled a dawn attack and then burned Prophetstown. The battle damaged the Prophet's prestige and pushed Tecumseh towards alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tippecanoe.jpg" alt="Battle of Tippecanoe" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kurtz &amp;amp; Allison, Popular Graphic Arts · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Tippecanoe_LCCN2003656861.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
